#: includes/class-jgor-flcf7-admin.php:728
msgid "Per placement"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-jgor-flcf7-admin.php:221
#: includes/class-jgor-flcf7-admin.php:729
msgid "Select the Contact Form 7 block, or a Shortcode block with the [contact-form-7] shortcode, and open the panel \"Floating Labels\" in the block sidebar. It stores the choice as classes in the \"Class\" field of the block (panel \"Form attributes\") or in the html_class attribute of the shortcode, so one form can look different on different pages. The panels \"Floating labels: colours\", \"Floating labels: sizes\" and \"Floating labels: animation\" below it hold design values for this placement only, stored with the block or in the jgor_flcf7_design attribute of the shortcode:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-jgor-flcf7-admin.php:223
#: includes/class-jgor-flcf7-admin.php:732
msgid "Per field"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-jgor-flcf7-admin.php:223
#: includes/class-jgor-flcf7-admin.php:733
msgid "Add the option nofloat to the form-tag, before any quoted value:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-jgor-flcf7-admin.php:233
msgid "Colours, sizes and timing are set in the section \"Design\" of this screen. Leave a field empty to keep the default; only the values you change are printed, as CSS custom properties on the .wpcf7 wrapper, right after the stylesheet."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-jgor-flcf7-admin.php:234
msgid "Themes can set the same properties in CSS, for example in Appearance > Customize > Additional CSS or a child theme. The snippet shows every property with the value in effect:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-jgor-flcf7-admin.php:236
msgid "To style one form only, replace .wpcf7 with the id of its wrapper, for example [id^=\"wpcf7-f123-\"], or with a class you add through the html_class attribute."
msgstr ""

